original:
There are five dangerous faults which may affect a general:
(1) Recklessness, which leads to destruction;
(2) cowardice, which leads to capture;
(3) a hasty temper, which can be provoked by insults;
(4) a delicacy of honour which is sensitive to shame;
(5) over-solicitude for his men, which exposes him to worry and trouble.

plain:
There are five dangerous faults a general can have:
(1) Recklessness, which leads to destruction;
(2) cowardice, which leads to capture;
(3) a quick temper, which can be provoked by insults;
(4) an oversensitive sense of honour that cannot bear shame;
(5) too much concern for his men, which exposes him to worry and trouble.
